.TH QSPACEMIDI 1 "August 2026" "qspacemidi 1.0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qspacemidi \- map a 3Dconnexion SpaceNavigator to MIDI CC messages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qspacemidi
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B QSpaceMIDI
turns the six degrees of freedom and the two buttons of a 3Dconnexion
SpaceNavigator 3D mouse into MIDI control change messages, so that the device
can drive parameters in Renoise or any other MIDI host.
.PP
The device is read directly from
.IR /dev/input/event* ,
so no proprietary 3DxWare driver is required.  A virtual ALSA sequencer port
named
.B QSpaceMIDI
is published for the host to connect to; an existing output port can be
selected instead.
.PP
Every axis has its own control change number, value mode and sensitivity.  A
global dead zone suppresses the resting jitter of the cap, and the axis lock
transmits only the axis that is deflected the most, which keeps parameters
from bleeding into each other while MIDI mapping in the host.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-minimized
Start hidden in the system tray.  The mapping is active even while the window
is not shown.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " file"
Render the window to
.I file
and exit.  Used to generate the documentation screenshot.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH DEFAULT MAPPING
.TS
tab(:);
l l l.
Axis:Direction:CC
_
X:left / right:1
Y:forward / backward:7
Z:up / down:74
RX:tilt left / right:10
RY:tilt forward / backward:71
RZ:rotate:91
Button 1:press:80
Button 2:press:81
.TE
.SH CC MODES
.TP
.B Absolute
The deflection itself, 0 to 127 with 64 at the centre.
.TP
.B Relative (Bin Offset)
64 means no change, 65 to 127 counts up, 63 to 1 counts down.
.TP
.B Relative (2's Comp)
1 to 63 counts up, 127 down to 65 counts down.
.TP
.B Relative (Signed Bit)
65 to 127 counts up, 1 to 63 counts down.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QSPACEMIDI_LANG
Language code overriding the system locale for one run, for example
.IR ja ", " de " or " zh_CN .
The interface ships in Danish, English, Finnish, French, German, Italian,
Japanese, Russian and Simplified Chinese.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/koppi/QSpaceMIDI.conf
Configuration, written through QSettings whenever a setting changes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/qspacemidi.desktop
Written and removed by the
.B Start at login
checkbox; starts the program minimised to the system tray.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99-spacenavigator.rules
udev rules that make the 3D mouse readable without root privileges.
.TP
.I /usr/share/icons/hicolor/scalable/status/qspacemidi-symbolic.svg
The monochrome tray icon.  Desktops that follow the status notifier protocol
are handed the name of this icon rather than a picture, so that they can draw
it from the icon theme; KDE recolours it to suit a light or a dark panel.
Set
.I tray/iconStyle
to
.IR monochrome " or " colour
to insist on one of the two, or leave it at
.I auto
to use the monochrome icon wherever the icon theme provides it.
.SH NOTES
Right click a row in the window to mute an axis or to reset its sensitivity;
the
.B \(+-
button at the end of a row inverts its direction.
.PP
Devices that report movement as deltas rather than as positions \- Linux
.B EV_REL
\- go quiet when the cap stops moving and never announce that it sprang back.
After
.I input/idleTimeout
milliseconds of silence \- 150 by default, 0 disables it \- their axes are
therefore treated as centred.  Devices that report absolute positions announce
the centre themselves and are left alone.
.PP
Between two CC updates the largest deflection seen is the one transmitted, so
a quick flick of the cap is not lost to the update rate.  On Linux the driver
also resynchronises with the device after
.BR SYN_DROPPED ,
where the kernel's event queue overflowed and events were genuinely lost.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aconnect (1),
.BR aseqdump (1)
